# --- SharePoint / OneDrive KB ingest (Microsoft Graph) ---
# Bearer access token for Microsoft Graph, read by the ingestion service at
# GraphClient construction time. SHAREPOINT_TOKEN is primary; GRAPH_TOKEN is
# the accepted fallback. Needs the Graph "Files.Read.All" permission (Azure AD
# app registration, or a token minted from Microsoft Graph Explorer). The
# Accepted link hosts: *.sharepoint.com, *.onedrive.com, *.sharepoint.us,
# onedrive.live.com, and 1drv.ms (OneDrive short links). The access token is
# short-lived (~1h) with NO auto-refresh — an expired token surfaces
# as HTTP 401 on ingest and must be replaced. Unlike the ADO PAT, this is a
# single shared SERVER identity (every KB ingest uses it), not per-user. Leave
# blank if not using SharePoint KB ingest — ingestion still boots; the
# /kb/ingest-url route just 400s until a token is set.
SHAREPOINT_TOKEN=
# GRAPH_TOKEN=            # fallback, only needed if SHAREPOINT_TOKEN is unset
# GRAPH_BASE_URL=         # optional override (default https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0)

# --- App auth: none. The ADO org URL + PAT (above) ARE the identity and the
# permissions (DocGen pattern) — no session/JWT, no separate identity
# provider. See docs/architecture.md "App auth" / CR4 of the corrected work
# plan for why the earlier JWT/Azure-AD scaffolding was removed.

# --- Infra ---
